# Graphify output is a DERIVED artifact — `graphify update .` rebuilds it from
# source (AST-only, no API cost), so git should not carry it.
#
# It was tracked until 2026-08-29. The cost: 79 MB in the working tree, 67 MB of
# it dated snapshot directories duplicating what git history already stores, and
# ~8.5M lines of churn in six weeks (graph.json alone: 8.8 MB, touched by 115
# commits). Nothing in CI or package.json ever read it. Worse, an 8.8 MB JSON
# blob regenerated on every commit conflicts unmergeably the moment two branches
# run in parallel — which is what the implement-epic skill does by design.
#
# README.md and cost.json stay tracked: near-static, and cost.json is the
# provenance record of what the graph build actually spent.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/README.md
!graphify-out/cost.json

# `**/` because a bare `graphify-out/cache/` anchors to the repo root and so
# missed the copy under server/ that `graphify update .` creates when it is
# run from inside a workspace.
**/graphify-out/cache/

# Build output (deployable artifact)
build-output/

